# DESIGN 1a: the four film-stage tables are derived from the declared exception's chain, so build.sh makes them
# (tools/mk_genesis_films.py stage) and they stay out of the history; films/tables/.genesis/ holds their cubes
films/tables/GX500T.T17
films/tables/GX250D.T17
films/tables/GXP400.T17
films/tables/GXE100.T17
films/tables/.genesis/
# the whole chain matrix (46 x 16, tools/mk_genesis_films.py matrix): 736 tables, ~14 MB, card data like the four above
films/tables/G[0-9][0-9]P[0-9][0-9].T17
films/tables/fit.csv
# the chain in two halves (tools/mk_wfstage.py): measured negative / print halves and pair placements, card data source
films/tables/.stage/
# option (c), the RAW develop's chain tables (tools/mk_genesis_films.py log): 643 x 215 KB, card data
films/tables/log/
# owner 11-16: a maker's wordmark (Canon_wordmark.svg and the like) stays in the owner's private folder; only our own
# test shape tests/host/logo_test.svg is tracked (*.DAT above keeps WFLOGO.DAT out)
*wordmark*
# owner 11-18: the Qwen hand-off files stay local only, never in the repo
# (copies in F:\MagicLatern\_windyfilm_docs\private\qwen_local; a pull that removes them can be restored from there)
/QWEN.md
/docs/*QWEN*.md
/docs/agents/
